[{:db/id "q-98326/selection/ebac00b083bb5c6203686ed587e4e856344ee99eed9580b3de89b1af058f6bda" :answer/id #uuid "497cd82c-2d94-5099-a900-434b458fbb38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.06" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98326/selection/74fac3c3b7f640d8df68b390884fbba043b56a6a841a7a89db00d34b47fb9ade" :answer/id #uuid "039035cb-0a1d-5d09-a999-bbc766ac3109" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98326/selection/8df0fb29b20ce0c5fcdbec7541c5eca6b2a012e69065d25d7a1f79cb0acf2256" :answer/id #uuid "01b5d356-4ec1-56b9-9410-d4d22c3b9d96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98326/selection/f7f72a13a2d3403453d18e5e8dafa0236126b621c900013d4538afdb17d2a33d" :answer/id #uuid "cfed4045-f8f3-57b5-9683-add678491a0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.08" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98326/selection/4ba07d595da94e6c18190f4c7e9ba4b4ed6a582ffd72c14b8d2af03cbda7a38b" :answer/id #uuid "0a72e800-6065-5b81-b422-d9da3e9826d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.92" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98326/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "deeeb20d-1e8d-548f-bb45-93126ea658d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-98326/selection/f7f72a13a2d3403453d18e5e8dafa0236126b621c900013d4538afdb17d2a33d" :answer-field/choices ["q-98326/selection/ebac00b083bb5c6203686ed587e4e856344ee99eed9580b3de89b1af058f6bda" "q-98326/selection/74fac3c3b7f640d8df68b390884fbba043b56a6a841a7a89db00d34b47fb9ade" "q-98326/selection/8df0fb29b20ce0c5fcdbec7541c5eca6b2a012e69065d25d7a1f79cb0acf2256" "q-98326/selection/f7f72a13a2d3403453d18e5e8dafa0236126b621c900013d4538afdb17d2a33d" "q-98326/selection/4ba07d595da94e6c18190f4c7e9ba4b4ed6a582ffd72c14b8d2af03cbda7a38b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-98326" :question/id #uuid "ea4d33e7-7c09-5d5e-9ccf-5bec677f88d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-98326" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(2,1)=2,\\,{f}_{x}(2,1)=-1,\\,{f}_{y}(2,1)=-1.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,1),$ estimate the value of $f(1.98,0.94).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(2,1)+∇f(2,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-1⟩ \\\\  & =f(2,1)+⟨{f}_{x}(2,1),{f}_{y}(2,1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-1⟩ \\\\  & =2+⟨-1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(1.98,0.94)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.98$ and $y=0.94,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.98,0.94) & ≈2+⟨-1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨1.98-2,0.94-1⟩ \\\\  & =2+⟨-1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.02,-0.06⟩ \\\\  & =2+(-1)(-0.02)+(-1)(-0.06) \\\\  & =2+0.02+0.06 \\\\  & =2.08\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-98326/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27e3c802-d356-5a2f-bdda-218144956722"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98326"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129637/selection/a29baf5bde025aa3e2d7e71015845c72eda5b8cff8b0de1fc25b75f9fa88f37b" :answer/id #uuid "19ace5d3-cace-5e78-a701-76bd57fc3430" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.08" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129637/selection/6c9efb9cf3a618d7bd09b074a65949edf3187d6c283606a48621efc3d9242c8e" :answer/id #uuid "becbcc96-86c2-5d37-bec2-864aa6793601" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.97" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129637/selection/26871791f536721d359b1584e59a0d164d9c9176a4ba072a1b14c7948e18a479" :answer/id #uuid "49aecb4a-dad0-5a2b-85d6-19b9a6d5ba6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129637/selection/327aacf725bedb2bb24a9e77847fcdc6f44bca836979b7277480c4b05863ef5a" :answer/id #uuid "e62457ba-0612-5aef-a2eb-f78e4a462739" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.99" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129637/selection/835679c6dd06e838074bcf99aeed8555bc3091f4818136537f6970a0279ab5a9" :answer/id #uuid "52813a06-58d8-5f29-bd42-9bfba352992f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.94" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129637/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "85ba5f1c-48bc-517a-9060-647184b38aa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129637/selection/6c9efb9cf3a618d7bd09b074a65949edf3187d6c283606a48621efc3d9242c8e" :answer-field/choices ["q-129637/selection/a29baf5bde025aa3e2d7e71015845c72eda5b8cff8b0de1fc25b75f9fa88f37b" "q-129637/selection/6c9efb9cf3a618d7bd09b074a65949edf3187d6c283606a48621efc3d9242c8e" "q-129637/selection/26871791f536721d359b1584e59a0d164d9c9176a4ba072a1b14c7948e18a479" "q-129637/selection/327aacf725bedb2bb24a9e77847fcdc6f44bca836979b7277480c4b05863ef5a" "q-129637/selection/835679c6dd06e838074bcf99aeed8555bc3091f4818136537f6970a0279ab5a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129637" :question/id #uuid "722c5cd7-1610-5083-b573-d3d05eef7bb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-129637" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,-1)=-2,\\,{f}_{x}(x,y)=2xy-{y}^{2},\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)={x}^{2}-2xy.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1),$ estimate the value of $f(0.95,-1.04).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(1,-1)+∇f(1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-(-1)⟩ \\\\  & ≈f(1,-1)+⟨{f}_{x}(1,-1),{f}_{y}(1,-1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1⟩ \\\\  & ≈-2+⟨{f}_{x}(1,-1),{f}_{y}(1,-1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(1,-1)$ and ${f}_{y}(1,-1)$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,-1) & =2(1)(-1)-(-1)^{2}=-3 \\\\ {f}_{y}(1,-1) & ={1}^{2}-2(1)(-1)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈-2+⟨-3,3⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(0.95,-1.04)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=0.95$ and $y=-1.04,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.95,-1.04) & ≈-2+⟨-3,3⟩\\cdot ⟨0.95-1,-1.04+1⟩ \\\\  & =-2+⟨-3,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.05,-0.04⟩ \\\\  & =-2-3(-0.05)+3(-0.04) \\\\  & =-2+0.15-0.12 \\\\  & =-1.97\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129637/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27e3c802-d356-5a2f-bdda-218144956722"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129637"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129632/selection/6f873079973074d0c2be24a6506582527e22f01ea61ff772a3d6692d849a66c0" :answer/id #uuid "a58fa64a-02a0-57fd-bb07-25f89f2e313c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.91" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129632/selection/2f74947e8dbc59523353f0f3e6b13789b3ce6900d5ff227939cab9d5d917eb22" :answer/id #uuid "ef59c749-e193-5e7c-9c7b-1032889d7ecf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.09" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129632/selection/27897cdf5ca18352e059100794a0a05fb42261f20455fff88a9a87deeb8a5a6a" :answer/id #uuid "a3068878-960b-5787-b74d-a95b430e4758" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.03" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129632/selection/590098bf0353bf8460aa1df224b73dd35e1164471ebb9d57b8cafd8270d254a4" :answer/id #uuid "5f3f193e-e83c-5782-a3df-93ee78a86b58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.06" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129632/selection/5ee3a691fab4cf4d2e29d2f3a7591a35cf29a2ee97fd68c1440d1d39998a5fad" :answer/id #uuid "442f0b3d-ca3b-517b-be61-b040cc120396" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.97" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129632/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b33762f2-a50d-51c3-9206-90ba7216864a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129632/selection/27897cdf5ca18352e059100794a0a05fb42261f20455fff88a9a87deeb8a5a6a" :answer-field/choices ["q-129632/selection/6f873079973074d0c2be24a6506582527e22f01ea61ff772a3d6692d849a66c0" "q-129632/selection/2f74947e8dbc59523353f0f3e6b13789b3ce6900d5ff227939cab9d5d917eb22" "q-129632/selection/27897cdf5ca18352e059100794a0a05fb42261f20455fff88a9a87deeb8a5a6a" "q-129632/selection/590098bf0353bf8460aa1df224b73dd35e1164471ebb9d57b8cafd8270d254a4" "q-129632/selection/5ee3a691fab4cf4d2e29d2f3a7591a35cf29a2ee97fd68c1440d1d39998a5fad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129632" :question/id #uuid "16a5abbe-ff57-5b9a-ab1e-16d413797e0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-129632" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,-1)=-3,\\,{f}_{x}(1,-1)=-6,\\,{f}_{y}(1,-1)=3.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1),$ estimate the value of $f(1.01,-0.99).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(1,-1)+∇f(1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =f(1,-1)+⟨{f}_{x}(1,-1),{f}_{y}(1,-1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1⟩ \\\\  & =-3+⟨-6,3⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(1.01,-0.99)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.01$ and $y=-0.99,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.01,-0.99) & ≈-3+⟨-6,3⟩\\cdot ⟨1.01-1,-0.99+1⟩ \\\\  & =-3+⟨-6,3⟩\\cdot ⟨0.01,0.01⟩ \\\\  & =-3-6(0.01)+3(0.01) \\\\  & =-3-0.06+0.03 \\\\  & =-3.03\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129632/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27e3c802-d356-5a2f-bdda-218144956722"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129632"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129636/selection/82e3ca489621df6bc2ddd93917e02938061ae326264283942bb1b32e942ab100" :answer/id #uuid "f545b7a8-d561-581f-8f9e-4ee3512e215f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.92" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129636/selection/67852d04a81963f731d37241714ec6c86e231c020cd7637662eee9bb41939292" :answer/id #uuid "a6ed3bd9-654a-526e-a5e8-911d195ef77a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129636/selection/8bf27e270a1a3307a867974d412c693c9d0219a2920a3e7cf912691884c37b5b" :answer/id #uuid "15a46d3c-9ce7-5186-878f-8a5555e987f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129636/selection/f4a245c67277507cb47495834519ff3373dec81fedcc0c0989b36f625d5a017e" :answer/id #uuid "6f09d95f-6a2f-54a5-8720-087796bc0ec9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.98" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129636/selection/da80db2015d51d051f8610a11897e4bce675d35a6d6d1866e6762dcf7fcec92a" :answer/id #uuid "c27539c1-159a-5b5c-a31f-7db508ef8511" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.04" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129636/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a02d405-095b-5898-bb69-b4ed45b0373a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129636/selection/67852d04a81963f731d37241714ec6c86e231c020cd7637662eee9bb41939292" :answer-field/choices ["q-129636/selection/82e3ca489621df6bc2ddd93917e02938061ae326264283942bb1b32e942ab100" "q-129636/selection/67852d04a81963f731d37241714ec6c86e231c020cd7637662eee9bb41939292" "q-129636/selection/8bf27e270a1a3307a867974d412c693c9d0219a2920a3e7cf912691884c37b5b" "q-129636/selection/f4a245c67277507cb47495834519ff3373dec81fedcc0c0989b36f625d5a017e" "q-129636/selection/da80db2015d51d051f8610a11897e4bce675d35a6d6d1866e6762dcf7fcec92a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129636" :question/id #uuid "3e7dfc5c-c144-5489-a8d0-c27c73e72883" :question/math-academy-id "q-129636" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,3)=4,\\,{f}_{x}(x,y)=2x+y,\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)=x.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,3),$ estimate the value of $f(1.04,3.03).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(1,3)+∇f(1,3)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-3⟩ \\\\  & ≈f(1,3)+⟨{f}_{x}(1,3),{f}_{y}(1,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-3⟩ \\\\  & ≈4+⟨{f}_{x}(1,3),{f}_{y}(1,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(1,3)$ and ${f}_{y}(1,3)$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,3) & =2(1)+3=5 \\\\ {f}_{y}(1,3) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈4+⟨5,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-3⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(1.04,3.03)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.04$ and $y=3.03,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.04,3.03) & ≈4+⟨5,1⟩\\cdot ⟨1.04-1,3.03-3⟩ \\\\  & =4+⟨5,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0.04,0.03⟩ \\\\  & =4+5(0.04)+1(0.03) \\\\  & =4+0.2+0.03 \\\\  & =4.23\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129636/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27e3c802-d356-5a2f-bdda-218144956722"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129636"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98344/selection/b60639d71f0964cc6247cf68198d91d7bfc85df3c95ec160d8c6fb7bfce7fac5" :answer/id #uuid "115ae366-e4b2-5b9d-803b-15cc78653af5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.04" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98344/selection/fbb177b5a3ba599fb8ab4d88a900e7589caf9e79c3a12254fa9118ba7d46b929" :answer/id #uuid "9a70f8c4-0580-5598-98d2-a7c1d3529d40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.84" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98344/selection/61c5d15ea0523c8a1f01509199218ed2a7006cabc3a7e335b1d7a4174bb7e981" :answer/id #uuid "81193eed-d5bf-5a37-9525-9749e07d51d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98344/selection/07c1a58330d2077ab0f7c539e4d52962dbc70067f1246fec1e6c5c2258a340d8" :answer/id #uuid "7966efe5-c29e-59c1-bfea-79dd3032d2b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98344/selection/97fc50414146d892e2751ad99f55154529a129934f8b9d1dbf8e1cb41399df45" :answer/id #uuid "ce0f1729-cb8d-5fcf-9310-362f020dd48f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98344/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "830a98bf-d229-53db-9248-dcecf3b8e9e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-98344/selection/07c1a58330d2077ab0f7c539e4d52962dbc70067f1246fec1e6c5c2258a340d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-98344/selection/b60639d71f0964cc6247cf68198d91d7bfc85df3c95ec160d8c6fb7bfce7fac5" "q-98344/selection/fbb177b5a3ba599fb8ab4d88a900e7589caf9e79c3a12254fa9118ba7d46b929" "q-98344/selection/61c5d15ea0523c8a1f01509199218ed2a7006cabc3a7e335b1d7a4174bb7e981" "q-98344/selection/07c1a58330d2077ab0f7c539e4d52962dbc70067f1246fec1e6c5c2258a340d8" "q-98344/selection/97fc50414146d892e2751ad99f55154529a129934f8b9d1dbf8e1cb41399df45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-98344" :question/id #uuid "e291dc27-d17d-5da1-907a-8c20b4b06f0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-98344" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & f(-3,-1,-2)=1, &  & {f}_{x}(-3,-1,-2)=4, \\\\  & {f}_{y}(-3,-1,-2)=-3, &  & {f}_{z}(-3,-1,-2)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-3,-1,-2)$ estimate the value of $f(-3.04,-1.02,-2.03).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-3,-1,-2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(-3,-1,-2)+∇f(-3,-1,-2)\\cdot ⟨x+3,y+1,z+2⟩ \\\\  & =f(-3,-1,-2) \\\\  & \\,+⟨{f}_{x}(-3,-1,-2),{f}_{y}(-3,-1,-2),{f}_{z}(-3,-1,-2)⟩\\cdot ⟨x+3,y+1,z+2⟩ \\\\  & =1+⟨4,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+3,y+1,z+2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-3.04,-1.02,-2.03)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=-3.04,$ $y=-1.02,$ and $z=-2.03$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3.04,-1.02,-2.03) & ≈1+⟨4,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3.04+3,-1.02+1,-2.03+2⟩ \\\\  & =1+⟨4,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.04,-0.02,-0.03⟩ \\\\  & =1-0.16+0.06+0.06 \\\\  & =0.96\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-98344/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1639105-dca4-50d1-8d86-a7aed03ba0b5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98344"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129661/selection/6c9efb9cf3a618d7bd09b074a65949edf3187d6c283606a48621efc3d9242c8e" :answer/id #uuid "20129a8f-9dd3-5c10-9cc8-a1d3415fa1dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.97" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129661/selection/cc7f5cf578566363e619693db366a6eee87614141653e51941ad14e4f0bf45b4" :answer/id #uuid "39eda29a-ea27-5aa1-b0f5-e6c79817307f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.04" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129661/selection/05f0f0ab18c9b247ae205defb05b3278dc07d5029b2916b639bddc2d71b86020" :answer/id #uuid "1a1322ae-e430-5629-91b0-4fa9cb4d578c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.03" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129661/selection/af4b0e8b2d62bd89db5789b403a660a562e541bada6c2f0e158a7339d7183ce0" :answer/id #uuid "1fa0adb4-1a7d-5b8b-bade-a90b105503fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.01" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129661/selection/327aacf725bedb2bb24a9e77847fcdc6f44bca836979b7277480c4b05863ef5a" :answer/id #uuid "9568e8d8-78e0-5e08-9b74-73c17a96dedc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.99" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129661/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "495c7a33-6298-5ac7-b2b1-ce8c34153360" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129661/selection/af4b0e8b2d62bd89db5789b403a660a562e541bada6c2f0e158a7339d7183ce0" :answer-field/choices ["q-129661/selection/6c9efb9cf3a618d7bd09b074a65949edf3187d6c283606a48621efc3d9242c8e" "q-129661/selection/cc7f5cf578566363e619693db366a6eee87614141653e51941ad14e4f0bf45b4" "q-129661/selection/05f0f0ab18c9b247ae205defb05b3278dc07d5029b2916b639bddc2d71b86020" "q-129661/selection/af4b0e8b2d62bd89db5789b403a660a562e541bada6c2f0e158a7339d7183ce0" "q-129661/selection/327aacf725bedb2bb24a9e77847fcdc6f44bca836979b7277480c4b05863ef5a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129661" :question/id #uuid "851c10b8-d992-54aa-ac89-df5795dc4190" :question/math-academy-id "q-129661" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(0,1,-1)=-2,\\,{f}_{x}(x,y,z)=z{e}^{x},\\,{f}_{y}(x,y,z)=-1,\\,{f}_{z}(x,y,z)={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,1,-1),$ estimate the value of $f(0.01,1.01,-0.99).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,1,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(0,1,-1)+∇f(0,1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-0,y-1,z-(-1)⟩ \\\\  & ≈-2+⟨{f}_{x}(0,1,-1),{f}_{y}(0,1,-1),{f}_{z}(0,1,-1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x,y-1,z+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(0,1,-1)$, ${f}_{y}(0,1,-1)$ and ${f}_{z}(0,1,-1),$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(0,1,-1) & =(-1){e}^{0}=-1 \\\\ {f}_{y}(0,1,-1) & =-1 \\\\ {f}_{z}(0,1,-1) & ={e}^{0}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈-2+⟨-1,-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,y-1,z+1⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(0.01,1.01,-0.99)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=0.01,y=1.01$ and $y=-0.99,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.01,1.01,-0.99) & ≈-2+⟨-1,-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0.01,1.01-1,-0.99+1⟩ \\\\  & ≈-2+⟨-1,-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0.01,0.01,0.01⟩ \\\\  & ≈-2-1(0.01)-1(0.01)+1(0.01) \\\\  & ≈-2-0.01-0.01+0.01 \\\\  & ≈-2.01\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129661/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1639105-dca4-50d1-8d86-a7aed03ba0b5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129661"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129655/selection/2e9e3484ea1eaa10dc34344b412e184b14c5c5c05b0f4e778abc52118e9d991c" :answer/id #uuid "074b5d17-1966-5602-a208-7d61a55fe866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.01" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129655/selection/2ee2cfe615154a44ab76e3add27527ea3aeb13df80b2aae862a301a9198678ea" :answer/id #uuid "760f544e-0628-525a-8251-c31e865fbb76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.02" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129655/selection/65828953f30eb965b7d80317d1875adc4cb9ddec9441b0d443889f21caf96f2d" :answer/id #uuid "39e99e97-023d-5ea3-92f3-933e829deb51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.98" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129655/selection/a52cfa8c15dc1ab8ca0f925c3aa1a4524cb69d8392bec863d93b373da38aa06a" :answer/id #uuid "01995fbd-842b-5fd2-be5b-65087f7de464" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.04" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129655/selection/06b5e2bdac9da5e6499ac156c110fc57d617507ae56bb3332d685f28f5cc5686" :answer/id #uuid "dc4350fc-cd39-55f9-88f7-6b03cd394f5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.97" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129655/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ccc4ee4-3761-518d-acc4-76247a58f8b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129655/selection/2ee2cfe615154a44ab76e3add27527ea3aeb13df80b2aae862a301a9198678ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-129655/selection/2e9e3484ea1eaa10dc34344b412e184b14c5c5c05b0f4e778abc52118e9d991c" "q-129655/selection/2ee2cfe615154a44ab76e3add27527ea3aeb13df80b2aae862a301a9198678ea" "q-129655/selection/65828953f30eb965b7d80317d1875adc4cb9ddec9441b0d443889f21caf96f2d" "q-129655/selection/a52cfa8c15dc1ab8ca0f925c3aa1a4524cb69d8392bec863d93b373da38aa06a" "q-129655/selection/06b5e2bdac9da5e6499ac156c110fc57d617507ae56bb3332d685f28f5cc5686"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129655" :question/id #uuid "fc7ad887-70cb-5594-8df2-c5717f843d45" :question/math-academy-id "q-129655" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(-1,1,0)=-1,\\,{f}_{x}(-1,1,0)=1,\\,{f}_{y}(-1,1,0)=-2,\\,{f}_{z}(-1,1,0)=0.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-1,1,0)$ estimate the value of $f(-1,1.01,-0.01)$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-1,1,0)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(-1,1,0)+∇f(-1,1,0)\\cdot ⟨x-(-1),y-1,z-0⟩ \\\\  & =f(-1,1,0)+⟨{f}_{x}(-1,1,0),{f}_{y}(-1,1,0),{f}_{z}(-1,1,0)⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,y-1,z⟩ \\\\  & =-1+⟨1,-2,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,y-1,z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-1,1.01,-0.01)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=-1,$ $y=1.01,$ and $z=-0.01$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1,1.01,-0.01) & ≈-1+⟨1,-2,0⟩\\cdot ⟨-1+1,1.01-1,-0.01⟩ \\\\  & =-1+⟨1,-2,0⟩\\cdot ⟨0,0.01,-0.01⟩ \\\\  & =-1+1(0)-2(0.01)+0(-0.01) \\\\  & =-1+0-0.02+0 \\\\  & =-1.02\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129655/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1639105-dca4-50d1-8d86-a7aed03ba0b5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129655"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36747"] :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x+y).$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(0,1)+∇f(0,1)\\cdot ⟨x,y-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(0,1)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =\\frac{1}{1+x+y}\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{x}(0,1)=\\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =\\frac{1}{1+x+y} &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{y}(0,1)=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(0,1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(0,1) & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(0,1)+∇f(0,1)\\cdot ⟨x,y-1⟩ \\\\  & ≈\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x,y-1⟩ \\\\  & ≈\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{y-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-98554/selection/8af3bc911afa0a19ddff90aadec01180d16e662cf5b25d2c8f169125d9f40a56" :answer/id #uuid "8b4724d5-c5d2-5523-88f1-5a62d4ce31ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-3+x-y+\\frac{z}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98554/selection/a21e519de66da66c34fdf95fab1f61a0296b3249bcbf50698526901085430691" :answer/id #uuid "9a4dd43e-e6bc-5d74-a641-91df1c9064a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-3+x-y-2z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98554/selection/246a0afccf89d26be6a50cd6910b39e02e26150f2d57a1fc94f7692ba29d3d89" :answer/id #uuid "4d74d46b-6884-58ee-bd81-cf6d47da9785" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-1+x+y-\\frac{z}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98554/selection/48999ec6243481be83718b1909f8f9ddfcefa9c9a5ca5d0155599d58ac01dbed" :answer/id #uuid "76c74212-a7f1-5863-afa4-dfc22129b560" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-1-x+y-2z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98554/selection/7d02f8b5eb7d37523f26f00ed3613e830ebd4fd504d689fd55d62c22b310c0cf" :answer/id #uuid "ea0408c7-99e8-5f0b-8756-0bc0fc4e9e64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈1-x+y-\\frac{z}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98554/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ece05490-41ce-5a5b-95af-f814f72055e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-98554/selection/246a0afccf89d26be6a50cd6910b39e02e26150f2d57a1fc94f7692ba29d3d89" :answer-field/choices ["q-98554/selection/8af3bc911afa0a19ddff90aadec01180d16e662cf5b25d2c8f169125d9f40a56" "q-98554/selection/a21e519de66da66c34fdf95fab1f61a0296b3249bcbf50698526901085430691" "q-98554/selection/246a0afccf89d26be6a50cd6910b39e02e26150f2d57a1fc94f7692ba29d3d89" "q-98554/selection/48999ec6243481be83718b1909f8f9ddfcefa9c9a5ca5d0155599d58ac01dbed" "q-98554/selection/7d02f8b5eb7d37523f26f00ed3613e830ebd4fd504d689fd55d62c22b310c0cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-98554" :question/id #uuid "f0a65ec3-c24d-50c1-a1d2-f9666a246122" :question/math-academy-id "q-98554" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=xy-\\operatorname{ln}⁡z.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,1,e).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,1,e)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,1,e)+∇f(1,1,e)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-1,z-e⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(1,1,e)=0.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =y\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{x}(1,1,e)=1, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =x\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{y}(1,1,e)=1, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =-\\frac{1}{z}\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{z}(1,1,e)=-\\frac{1}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(1,1,e)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(1,1,e) & =⟨1,1,-\\frac{1}{e}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,1,e)+∇f(1,1,e)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-1,z-e⟩ \\\\  & =0+⟨1,1,-\\frac{1}{e}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-1,z-e⟩ \\\\  & =0+1(x-1)+1(y-1)-\\frac{1}{e}(z-e) \\\\  & =-1+x+y-\\frac{z}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-98554/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0015e19e-222b-5c5b-a020-93392c50c10e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98554"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98551/selection/4d92d77f30563b7ac67a80025d42fdc4bf000a8ca85e8eaba1030f9208d5c17f" :answer/id #uuid "5df35a1e-5afa-5cc0-8391-941ebc0f1dc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈2x+\\frac{y}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98551/selection/3b79c4c826558decacc8efc445f71d66a7ba699c6a179997b0b63424d635edda" :answer/id #uuid "c34967f9-9b3f-5690-b5ac-b2c3c64e7a9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈16+2x+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98551/selection/ed1815deb234cfa07e6c583862aa75733bf3e3915fe4066971b484d24b0d683c" :answer/id #uuid "3e2510ee-62d1-50fb-acc2-214392fa1bd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈16+2x+\\frac{y}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98551/selection/09f4249cb75f0ba26ba45ed1c95c6967f819141d9ed8b33bf9db5c4adafddd00" :answer/id #uuid "3ba8fb6d-3a05-5c68-94a7-afc4fd13f558" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈\\frac{x}{2}+2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98551/selection/eca1880638cb70e586836a349c96a6bb3be10eff2636facbb8d1029163463597" :answer/id #uuid "7c95ec5f-6cc6-5b77-bf20-a9d5f5c26f30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈\\frac{x}{2}+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98551/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "70f953ec-0ee9-5cad-9b70-336e5ef135b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-98551/selection/4d92d77f30563b7ac67a80025d42fdc4bf000a8ca85e8eaba1030f9208d5c17f" :answer-field/choices ["q-98551/selection/4d92d77f30563b7ac67a80025d42fdc4bf000a8ca85e8eaba1030f9208d5c17f" "q-98551/selection/3b79c4c826558decacc8efc445f71d66a7ba699c6a179997b0b63424d635edda" "q-98551/selection/ed1815deb234cfa07e6c583862aa75733bf3e3915fe4066971b484d24b0d683c" "q-98551/selection/09f4249cb75f0ba26ba45ed1c95c6967f819141d9ed8b33bf9db5c4adafddd00" "q-98551/selection/eca1880638cb70e586836a349c96a6bb3be10eff2636facbb8d1029163463597"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-98551" :question/id #uuid "3f4fd5df-dadd-52f6-b149-36a5758ba585" :question/math-academy-id "q-98551" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=2\\sqrt{xy}.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,8).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,8)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(2,8)+∇f(2,8)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(2,8)=8.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{x}(2,8)=\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 8}}=2, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{xy}} &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{y}(2,8)=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 8}}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(2,8)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(2,8) & =⟨2,\\frac{1}{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(2,8)+∇\\,f(2,8)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-8⟩ \\\\  & =8+⟨2,\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-8⟩ \\\\  & =8+2(x-2)+\\frac{1}{2}(y-8) \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{y}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-98551/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0015e19e-222b-5c5b-a020-93392c50c10e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98551"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129748/selection/78378c8c4baa77f9a9c2864316bcbc98ca1ed78920d3c9a95ae326e2c30efad0" :answer/id #uuid "72d635ea-d802-53ae-81c1-0f633e0575e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-2y+z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129748/selection/54b0f761d1f204ee0cd1fc089a958ba8627c4b8d1c7c73e29991b8642ae8e3b5" :answer/id #uuid "c7fc4900-f94d-512a-81e9-bae99e9605ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈1+x+z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129748/selection/321ca6e26537bf1b7a1d3c40e7d13453b865feb402b312de7fde4bd42d86b4e7" :answer/id #uuid "21943c76-a14b-5c48-843e-92d06b0a7737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈2+x+y+z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129748/selection/585f615ecccbcf582093630d701d825f492f5b805cf626672b5eeaf3fcc76526" :answer/id #uuid "ce1e83fe-f2e5-5a1b-82de-f56b614ba214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈2+x+2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129748/selection/024536d935675eb659a721ec3fe7699b4832a2019168b4ea0049ad6859c6bf7e" :answer/id #uuid "943bbf47-0de5-5945-9649-ae7bf940998d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-2+x-y-z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129748/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "622e5437-cc3a-5c20-992b-b46594be4c14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129748/selection/024536d935675eb659a721ec3fe7699b4832a2019168b4ea0049ad6859c6bf7e" :answer-field/choices ["q-129748/selection/78378c8c4baa77f9a9c2864316bcbc98ca1ed78920d3c9a95ae326e2c30efad0" "q-129748/selection/54b0f761d1f204ee0cd1fc089a958ba8627c4b8d1c7c73e29991b8642ae8e3b5" "q-129748/selection/321ca6e26537bf1b7a1d3c40e7d13453b865feb402b312de7fde4bd42d86b4e7" "q-129748/selection/585f615ecccbcf582093630d701d825f492f5b805cf626672b5eeaf3fcc76526" "q-129748/selection/024536d935675eb659a721ec3fe7699b4832a2019168b4ea0049ad6859c6bf7e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129748" :question/id #uuid "15c1d2a5-42db-5b28-be3e-79c32c67c3c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-129748" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=xyz.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,-1,-1)+∇f(1,-1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1,z+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(1,-1,-1)=1.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =yz\\,⇒\\,{f}_{x}(1,-1,-1)=1, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =xz\\,⇒\\,{f}_{y}(1,-1,-1)=-1, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =xy\\,⇒\\,{f}_{z}(1,-1,-1)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(1,-1,-1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(1,-1,-1) & =⟨{f}_{x}(1,-1,-1),{f}_{y}(1,-1,-1),{f}_{z}(1,-1,-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,-1,-1)+∇f(1,-1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1,z+1⟩ \\\\  & ≈1+⟨1,-1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1,z+1⟩ \\\\  & ≈1+(x-1)-(y+1)-(z+1) \\\\  & ≈-2+x-y-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-129748/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0015e19e-222b-5c5b-a020-93392c50c10e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129748"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
